  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CORE FUNDING 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since its foundation in 1999, Medicines for Malaria Venture (MMV) has delivered on its mission to reduce the burden of malaria in disease-endemic countries, especially in vulnerable and under-served populations, by discovering, developing and facilitating delivery of new, effective and affordable antimalarial drugs. Today, MMV manages a portfolio of over 65 antimalarial medicines, the largest ever assembled. With partners, they have launched 15 medicines that are treating patients and to-date have saved over 3 million lives. Ireland&apos;s grant supports: Enhancing the level of control that can be achieved with current treatment options, developing new tools to support elimination and eradication, especially in the face of growing resistance in Africa and bringing forward tools and strategies to prevent resurgence.</narrative>
  </description>
